{"availability":"available","full":"hassanalsa3aka/devora.js","name":"devora.js","description":"A Vite-based React framework with native multi-app support — one repo, several independently-deployed apps sharing a core.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-06T23:57:38Z","updated":"2026-10-15T23:29:38Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://devorajs-docs-docs.vercel.app","topics":["framework","multi-app","netlify","react","ssr","typescript","vercel","vite"],"demo":"https://devorajs-docs-docs.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T00:57:36.358Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T00:57:36.358Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T00:57:36.358Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T04:07:35.966Z","stars":6,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T00:57:36.358Z","stars":6,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Vite-based React framework built around one idea : a project is more than one app.","Devora.js lets you define several apps in one repo — a marketing site, a product app, an admin panel — that share a core and a backend, but build and deploy independently. Each app gets its own render mode, its own auth mode, and its own deploy target, without duplicating the plumbing between them.","Most React frameworks assume one app per project. The moment a real product needs a marketing site, a product app, and an admin panel — a pretty normal shape — you're either cramming them into one app with route groups, or maintaining separate repos that share nothing. Devora.js treats \"one repo, several independently-deployed apps sharing a core\" as the default, not a workaround bolted on later."],"features":["Multi-app, one repo — devora.config.ts declares each app; devora build/devora deploy","handle each one independently.","SSR, SSG, CSR, ISR, streaming — set per route, explicitly. Streaming is GET-only (no","action), and on Netlify it's delivered as on